# kills: the deck-chip strip stays clear of the sidebar with several custom decks
# suite: node --test --test-name-pattern ^the.deck.chip.strip.stays.clear.of.the.sidebar.with.several.custom.decks$ tests/e2e.test.js
# Reviewer finding F1: drops the desktop-only header{max-width:...} override
# added inside the @media(min-width:1024px) block. Without it, header falls
# back to the 640px-only rule (max-width:min(92vw,900px)), which at
# >=1024px runs out to the right far enough to sit under the fixed 240px
# sidebar - the deck-chip strip's selected chip is hidden behind the
# sidebar and elementFromPoint at its centre returns a sidebar control
# instead.
# Context refreshed 2026-09-29 (M3b, round-2 follow-up, Q19): the rule this
# mutant drops now reads `min(900px, calc(100vw - 480px - 2 * var(--sp-3)))`
# instead of the bare calc() - a second reviewer finding (Q19) wrapped it in
# min() so it also respects the base rule's 900px ceiling at very wide
# viewports. The mutation is unchanged in kind: it still removes the whole
# header max-width override, which is what this test actually exercises.
diff --git a/index.html b/index.html
--- a/index.html
+++ b/index.html
@@ -265,7 +265,6 @@
      900px cap the base rule exists to enforce. Keep both limits - the
      900px ceiling and the sidebar clearance - by taking the smaller of the
      two, the same min() shape the base rule already uses. */
-  header{max-width:min(900px, calc(100vw - 480px - 2 * var(--sp-3)))}
   #settings-panel{
     /* top/bottom inset var(--sp-1), not 0: the page-background test's outer
        frame (tests/e2e.test.js "page background covers every viewport")
